<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Culture &amp; Lifestyle</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-cul</id><updated>2026-09-09T13:03:15Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-cul" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1441?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-cul" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>The Bayeux Tapestry in London: What's behind the hype?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:42e18cd84e1dc5e66d6ee277d71fa68b969c41faaab6cce1219c938da6cdbbb0</id><updated>2026-09-09T13:03:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T07:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-bayeux-tapestry-in-london-what-s-behind-the-hype/a-78488629--9a9477f8929c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-bayeux-tapestry-in-london-what-s-behind-the-hype/a-78488629?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The exhibition of the Bayeux Tapestry at the British Museum is eagerly anticipated across the UK, as the medieval masterpiece is considered by many to be a symbol of the country's identity.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Merz, Weidel face off after AfD state win</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4e4ad03064b6bc2e145ed5a95f4bfd6fc4d228f932cbdad96bb8124e0bd5e6e5</id><updated>2026-09-09T13:02:56Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T08:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-weidel-face-off-after-afd-state-win/live-79196246--7057d0c40f30.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-weidel-face-off-after-afd-state-win/live-79196246?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Alice Weidel and Friedrich Merz traded barbs the Bundestag days after the AfD's victory in Saxony-Anhalt has put new pressure on the German chancellor. DW has the latest.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Renoir Museum robbery: 2 paintings missing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ebbf1e1563697d0c529bcbca64cc2c1df9962aa4ef929cbf77bfba228264c636</id><updated>2026-09-09T13:01:47Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T07:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/renoir-museum-robbery-2-paintings-missing/a-79154458--4fcf4fff5ab0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/renoir-museum-robbery-2-paintings-missing/a-79154458?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Police are on the hunt for thieves who stole two paintings from the Renoir Museum on the French Riviera in an overnight heist. Two other stolen works were abandoned as they fled.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: From emigration to immigration destination</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cb2ae01da0f689c349308c3c5aff89bb5f7de34bcee901147b7d544677753388</id><updated>2026-09-09T13:01:47Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T08:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-from-emigration-to-immigration-destination/a-78805541--ac3bd047b864.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-from-emigration-to-immigration-destination/a-78805541?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Migration is a sensitive topic in Germany, with public debate dominated by the fear of uncontrolled immigration. But over two centuries, millions of Germans emigrated in search of a better life.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Werner Herzog: Germany's wild man of cinema is back</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c23224f00e8254ded9bb7637d1b97d5df8e810b8ceed715bc379721519f62128</id><updated>2026-09-09T13:01:47Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T16:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/werner-herzog-germany-s-wild-man-of-cinema-is-back/a-78949324--4a5372e58812.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/werner-herzog-germany-s-wild-man-of-cinema-is-back/a-78949324?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As his latest movie, "Bucking Fastard," premiered at the Venice Film Festival, DW talked to the boundary-breaking director.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>This extremely successful author polarizes German readers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ae1210e49270c6443f47d2f6eb7020abe60c30ab8dd1ec06f4c6aaf45ab8ee69</id><updated>2026-09-09T13:01:47Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T07:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/this-extremely-successful-author-polarizes-german-readers/a-78500452--1ca180b39c00.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/this-extremely-successful-author-polarizes-german-readers/a-78500452?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">She's young and she says what she thinks: Caroline Wahl is topping Germany's bestseller lists with her novels. But she has also faced a public backlash.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Japan's empty temples seek new ways to survive</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1cfb973b78098ae8bb9f061f7f0d3a1c6ea3347a5cd5c1a4639fd5f7f0d0229b</id><updated>2026-09-09T13:01:47Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T12:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/japan-s-empty-temples-seek-new-ways-to-survive/a-79157964--7eea677a26bf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/japan-s-empty-temples-seek-new-ways-to-survive/a-79157964?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">With a declining population, shrinking congregations and growing economic pressures, temples are struggling to stay relevant. As more temples are sold or closed, is religion in decline in modern Japan?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>PISA 2025 results: Reading and math scores plummet worldwide</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:90ab079e9f2dac5da71299fbf4cec98c7d988a3c5a1c3b5074b146288e5dac08</id><updated>2026-09-09T13:03:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T07:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pisa-test-reveals-alarming-drop-in-reading-and-math-skills/a-79147293--6fcb0a53f051.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pisa-2025-results-reading-and-math-scores-plummet-worldwide/a-79147293?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The PISA 2025 results reveal record-low student performance, with digital distractions and AI use raising concerns. Germany is faring worse than ever.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Bauhaus Manifesto: Broad alliance promoting artistic freedom</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dcf63999e9251109eee8f22b2ec5abab8708c60530014dedd1caf446812da8b8</id><updated>2026-09-09T13:01:47Z</updated><published>2026-08-21T10:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bauhaus-manifesto-broad-alliance-promoting-artistic-freedom/a-78456460--2d3d86ae9554.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bauhaus-manifesto-broad-alliance-promoting-artistic-freedom/a-78456460?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Weeks before Saxony-Anhalt's state election, representatives from German cultural, crafts, architecture, design and church sectors unite to promote freedom, openness and creativity.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Hunger stones: The history behind 'if you see me, weep'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:543fe6fc2c925dfb7e7e29af5bca06f651aa70dcb52435f062ab87892e250a8a</id><updated>2026-09-09T13:01:47Z</updated><published>2026-08-14T07:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/hunger-stones-the-history-behind-if-you-see-me-weep/a-78345729--34d8ccc8292a.html